    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0444" n="340" xml:id="pg340"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Lincoln.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 21,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 267.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 229 of the 5th instant,
                    concerning your interview with Lord Salisbury with reference to the resumption
                    of diplomatic relations between Great Britain and Venezuela, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>The substance of your dispatch has been communicated to the Venezuelan minister
                    at this capital and a copy thereof transmitted to our minister at Caracas for
                    his information.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
